{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## rebar-debug Phase 2 report — fix, tests, replication\n\nChange: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1494\n\n### What changed\n\n**The fix (one line at one chokepoint).** `llm/config.py:_read_llm_file_table` now defaults its\n`repo_root` to `current_code_root()` when the caller threads none. Both readers that mattered —\n`model_classes.load_class_slots` and `LLMConfig.from_env`'s own table read — land there, so the\nclass table and the scalar `cfg.model` are fixed together. An explicit `repo_root` still wins\n(threading never becomes a no-op) and outside a gate `current_code_root()` is `None`, so ambient\ndiscovery is byte-identical.\n\n**Sibling threading.** Call sites holding an `LLMConfig` now thread `cfg.repo_path`:\n`config.resolve_model`, `overlap/judge.py` (x2), `completion.py`, `plan_review/__init__.py`,\n`enrich.py`, `epic_bug_screen.py`, `code_review/workflow_ops.py`, and `runner.py`'s two slot\nlookups (`fallback_targets_for` / `primary_endpoint_for` gained an optional `repo_root`).\n`plan_review/sizing.py:382` is deliberately NOT threaded and says so: an existing test\nmonkeypatches `models_at_or_above` as a one-argument callable, and the chokepoint fix already\ncovers that path.\n\n**Documentation of the operator decision.** The \"deliberately blanks ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\" note is\nnow explicitly scoped to the PROVIDER MATRIX in `.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml`,\n`rebar.toml`, and `docs/local-dev-env.md`, so it is not re-litigated a fourth time.\n\n### Tests — RED first, held out, mutation-checked\n\n`tests/unit/test_llm_config_gate_root.py` (new, 7 tests). All were observed RED for the right\nreason before any fix existed; the fix was written by a subagent that never saw the file (it was\nmoved out of the tree, not merely omitted from the prompt); re-seeding the exact defect returns\nall 5 mechanism tests to RED.\n\nThey run over the REAL discovery path — a real `rebar.toml` on disk, process cwd in a git repo\nthat is deliberately NOT a rebar project. That matters: the pre-existing\n`tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py` monkeypatches `_read_llm_file_table`, i.e. it stubs out\nthe exact layer that was broken, which is why a 504-line fallback suite was blind to this.\n\nThe end-to-end fallback test asserts the caller **RECEIVED the fallback's answer**\n(`_answer(result) == \"answered-by-<fallback>\"`) plus the attestation naming it — not merely that\na fallback was attempted. That distinction is the point: the reported failure mode (attempt ->\n401 -> misleading error) would PASS an attempt-only assertion. A differential partner test pins\nthat a healthy primary does NOT fail over, so a fix that routed everything to the fallback cannot\npass both.\n\n### Replication — the original report no longer reproduces\n\nRe-running the reported condition (active gate code root, cwd outside the project), both\noperations named in the report now bind Bedrock:\n\n    plan-review verifier cfg.model = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\n    overlap-judge bound model      = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\n    enrich/epic-screen bound model = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0\n    completion verifier model      = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\n\nBefore the fix all four resolved to bare-Anthropic ids; `anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6` is the exact\nstring in the 401.\n\n### What this change deliberately does NOT do, and why\n\n**It does not enable the `fallback` chain in `rebar.toml`.** I implemented that (it is what the\noperator approved), measured it, and backed it out — see [rebar:8fbd-e9d5-326e-40d8], filed and\nlinked `discovered_from` this ticket. Two blockers, both measured here:\n\n1. A chain makes the runner resolve capabilities as the CONSERVATIVE INTERSECTION across its\n   candidates (`runner.py:441`). `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` is MEASURED\n   native-structured-output-capable ([rebar:18ae]) while its direct-Anthropic twin deliberately\n   stays PromptedOutput. Enabling the arm therefore moves EVERY standard-class call from native\n   to prompted output project-wide — silently undoing a measured decision as a side effect of a\n   resilience change. `tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py` catches it\n   (`assert (True, True) == (True, False)`); I left it to catch it rather than relaxing it.\n2. The credential does not work (below).\n\nTurning on a project-wide provider chain with a measured capability regression is a design\ndecision, not a bug fix, so it does not ride along on this one.\n\n### OPERATOR ACTION REQUIRED — the ANTHROPIC_API_KEY on this host is invalid\n\nThis is the part no coding session can fix, and it is independent of the code defect above.\n`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` **is** set on the development host (108 chars, `sk-ant-` prefix) and is\nrejected by Anthropic:\n\n    GET https://api.anthropic.com/v1/models  ->  HTTP 401\n    {\"type\":\"authentication_error\",\"message\":\"API key is invalid.\"}\n\nSo the ticket's second hypothesis (\"the credential is simply absent/invalid\") is confirmed for\nthe credential itself — but note it was NOT the cause of the reported 401s' existence. The calls\nshould never have gone to direct Anthropic at all; the invalid key is why they failed loudly\nrather than silently costing money on the wrong provider.\n\nNo attempt was made to obtain, guess, or substitute a key. What is needed: provision a valid\n`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` for local/CI operation and verify it with the one-line probe now documented\nin `docs/local-dev-env.md`. Until then the approved fallback arm cannot be enabled\n([rebar:8fbd-e9d5-326e-40d8] blocker 2).\n\nNote also that `should_fall_back` deliberately excludes credential failures (`CHANGE_SETTINGS`) —\n\"a credential error must not be masked by shopping for a provider whose key happens to work\" — so\nno fallback chain will ever rescue a bad key. The key has to be valid.\n\n### Residual risk\n\n- `plan_review/sizing.py` and `plan_review/prerequisites.py` keep ambient class resolution for\n  the explicit-`repo_path`-without-a-gate case, blocked by a one-argument monkeypatch in\n  `test_plan_review_prerequisites_model_log.py`. ACCEPTED in scope (the gate case, which is the\n  reported one, is fixed); noted here so the next reader knows it is a known edge, not an\n  oversight.\n- Pre-fix measurements of provider latency and of overlap-judge failures are contaminated by this\n  misroute. Commented on [rebar:1e88] and [rebar:2391] respectively."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786102463215677001,"uuid":"e3428bcc-6a24-423c-890d-257deb337280"}